# How many Earths would fit inside the Sun?
subtitle: "Guess how many Earths would fit inside the Sun on a line where every step is ten times bigger, then see why the answer runs into millions."
voices: {"a":"gemini:Iapetus | a clear space quiz host; quiet wonder, natural pace","take":"lines"}

## How many Earths would fit inside the Sun?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: nasa
      title: 'Sun: Facts'
      authors: NASA Science
      year: 2024
      url: https://science.nasa.gov/sun/facts/
      finding: the Sun is about 109 times as wide as Earth; about 1.3 million Earths would fit inside it; it holds 99.8 % of the solar system's mass

    card title "How many Earths fit in the Sun?"

How many Earths would fit inside the Sun?
    ellipse sun #d08a1e x 270 y 415 rx 228 ry 228 style.fill #f2c14e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.5
    text sun_l "Sun" #b5482e x 270 y 415 font_size 64

Here is the Earth beside it, drawn to scale: that tiny dot.
    ellipse earth #2f6b8f x 560 y 415 rx 2.1 ry 2.1 style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 1
    arrow earth_arrow #2f6b8f from.x 650 from.y 500 to.x 567 to.y 422
    text earth_l "Earth, to scale" #2f6b8f x 770 y 530 font_size 42

Make your guess on this line. Each step along it is ten times the last.
    scale n cites ["nasa"] x 530 y 250 width 400 min 10 max 10000000 value 1300000 log true

    ask "How many Earths would fit inside the Sun? Click on the line." on n store g default "10000"
        right: Close: about one point three million.
        wrong: It is about one point three million.

    erase earth_arrow earth_l

The Sun is a hundred and nine times as wide as the Earth.
    text wide "109 × wider" #b5482e cites ["nasa"] x 735 y 600 font_size 52

And volume grows with the cube: a hundred and nine, times a hundred and nine, times a hundred and nine.
    math cube tex "109^3 \\approx 1{,}300{,}000" size 34 x 735 y 500

That makes about one point three million Earths, if you could melt them down to fill every gap.
    highlight cube

The Sun also holds about 99.8 percent of all the mass in the solar system.
    text mass "99.8 % of the mass" #2f6b8f cites ["nasa"] x 760 y 395 font_size 38

So everything else, Jupiter and us included, is crumbs.
    highlight earth effect circle
